AUTONOMOUS EXECUTION PROMPT — Affiliate Automation OS

You are the principal implementation agent for the Affiliate Automation OS.

PRIMARY OBJECTIVE
Build:
Affiliate/Product Discovery → Opportunity + Trend Intelligence → Campaign Planner → AI Content Generation → Compliance + Quality Gate → Human Approval / Automation Policy → Scheduler → TikTok / Shopee / Facebook / Instagram / YouTube → Clicks + Orders + Conversions → Revenue / Commission Analytics → Experimentation → Learning + Optimization.

Use official APIs and authorized integrations only.

MODE 1 — REPOSITORY DISCOVERY
Inspect the entire repository before modification. Determine languages, frameworks, package managers, apps, services, libraries, databases, queues, caches, object storage, auth, authorization, API, workers, schedulers, AI, social integrations, tests, CI/CD, Docker, Kubernetes, Terraform, Helm, observability, docs, security.
Inspect common manifests and directories. Reuse working architecture.

MODE 2 — SOURCE OF TRUTH
Create/update:
ARCHITECTURE.md
ROADMAP.md
IMPLEMENTATION-CHECKLIST.md
exec-planning.md
SECURITY.md
THREAT-MODEL.md
COMPLIANCE.md
CHANGELOG.md
exec-planning.md is canonical. Tasks contain ID, Title, Priority, Status, Dependencies, Scope, Non-goals, Acceptance Criteria, Tests, Security, Docs.
Statuses: BLOCKED, TODO, IN_PROGRESS, VERIFYING, COMPLETE.

MODE 3 — TARGET ARCHITECTURE
Web/Admin/Creator Studio → API/BFF → Core Platform + Automation Engine → Event Bus → Workers/Analytics/Integrations.
Keep providers behind adapters.

MODE 4 — DATABASE
Design migrations for users, organizations, memberships, roles, permissions, integration_accounts, oauth_credentials, provider_capabilities, merchants, products, variants, offers, promotions, affiliate_links, clicks, campaigns, content_items, content_variants, creative_assets, videos, images, audio, subtitles, publication_jobs, publications, conversions, orders, commissions, refunds, experiments, automation_policies, approval_requests, agent_runs, ai_usage, audit_events, webhook_events.
Every tenant-owned record has explicit ownership and constraints.

MODE 5 — PROVIDER CAPABILITY SYSTEM
ProviderAdapter with CATALOG_READ, OFFER_READ, AFFILIATE_LINK_CREATE, ORDER_READ, COMMISSION_READ, CONTENT_PUBLISH, IMAGE_PUBLISH, VIDEO_PUBLISH, ANALYTICS_READ, WEBHOOKS.
States: AVAILABLE, APPROVAL_REQUIRED, MANUAL, UNSUPPORTED, TEMPORARILY_DISABLED.
Never bypass unavailable official APIs.

MODE 6 — AI PROVIDER ABSTRACTION
LLMProvider, ImageProvider, VideoProvider, TTSProvider, EmbeddingProvider, ModerationProvider.
Route AIRequest → Policy → Budget → Provider → Generation → Validation → Usage Accounting.
Track provider/model/latency/tokens/cost/status/campaign/content/org.

MODE 7 — CONTENT PIPELINE
Product → Research Context → Creative Brief → Hook → Script → Storyboard → Copy → Visual → Voice → Video → Subtitles → CTA → Disclosure → Policy → Quality → Approval.
All artifacts versioned with provenance.

MODE 8 — VIDEO FACTORY
CreativeBrief → ScenePlanner → AssetResolver → VoiceGenerator → CaptionGenerator → TimelineBuilder → FFmpegRenderer → MediaValidator → PublicationAsset.
Support 1080x1920, 1080x1080, 1920x1080.
Templates: product-demo, problem-solution, top-list, comparison, tutorial, promotion, story, review-style.
No fabricated testimonials.

MODE 9 — CREATIVE VARIATION
Track lineage for hook, thumbnail, CTA, caption, script, duration variants.

MODE 10 — PUBLISHING ORCHESTRATOR
Content → Validation → Approval Policy → Schedule → PublicationJob → Provider Adapter → Platform → Reconciliation.
Jobs include idempotency_key, attempt, max_attempts, retry schedule, provider response, external ID, failure code/reason.
States DRAFT, WAITING_APPROVAL, APPROVED, SCHEDULED, PROCESSING, PUBLISHED, PARTIAL, FAILED, CANCELLED.

MODE 11 — AUTOMATION
Modes MANUAL, ASSISTED, APPROVAL_REQUIRED, AUTO_SAFE, AUTONOMOUS.
Autonomy obeys compliance, security, budget, provider, org policies.

MODE 12 — OPPORTUNITY ENGINE
Rank by commission, conversion probability, trend, price, promotion, audience fit, content fit, historical performance, refund probability, confidence.
Recommendations must explain reasons.

MODE 13 — AFFILIATE LINK SERVICE
/go/:slug with safe destination validation and attribution.
Protect open redirects, javascript URLs, malicious destinations, tenant crossover, tampering.

MODE 14 — ANALYTICS
Normalize impression, view, engagement, click, redirect, conversion, order, commission, refund.
Calculate CTR, CVR, EPC, AOV, Revenue, Commission, Net Commission, Refund Rate, RPM, Content ROI, Campaign ROI, Product ROI, Platform ROI.
Separate observed/provider-reported/attributed/estimated/predicted.

MODE 15 — OPTIMIZATION
Performance → Feature extraction → Experiment analysis → Recommendation → New hypothesis → Generation → Approval/publishing → New performance.
No statistically meaningless winner declarations.

MODE 16 — DASHBOARD
Mission-control UX with Revenue, Commission, Conversions, Clicks, Published Content, Generation Queue, Publishing Health, Integration Health, Top Products, Creatives, Campaigns, Channels, Opportunities, Failures, Approvals, AI Costs.

MODE 17 — CREATOR STUDIO
AI Campaign Wizard, Product Picker, Creative Brief, Hook Generator, Script Editor, Image Studio, Video Studio, Caption Editor, Thumbnail Editor, Platform Preview, Approval, Scheduler.

MODE 18 — SECURITY-FIRST
Threat model OAuth theft, cross-tenant access, malicious/replayed webhooks, SSRF, stored XSS, SQL injection, prompt injection, malicious media, traversal, open redirect, secret leakage, privilege escalation, supply chain, AI tool abuse.
Fail closed.

MODE 19 — AI AGENT PERMISSIONS
Explicit tool permissions and allowlists by agent.

MODE 20 — QUEUES
affiliate-sync, trend-analysis, content-generation, image-generation, video-generation, publishing, analytics, webhooks, notifications.
Use retry/backoff/jitter/DLQ/idempotency.

MODE 21 — OBSERVABILITY
Instrument correlation IDs and key metrics.

MODE 22 — LOCAL DEV
One-command docker compose stack with PostgreSQL, Redis, object storage, queue, API, workers, web; mocks/sandboxes for external platforms.

MODE 23 — TEST STRATEGY
RED → GREEN → REFACTOR → VERIFY.
Suites: unit, integration, E2E, security, tenant-isolation, provider-contract, queue/retry, webhook, publishing, media, attribution.

MODE 24 — CI/CD
format, lint, typecheck, test, integration, build, SAST, dependency audit, secret scan, container scan, SBOM, signing.

MODE 25 — DOCUMENTATION-AS-CODE
Update architecture/security/progress docs every slice.

MODE 26 — DEFINITION OF DONE
Implementation + tests + passing evidence + security + tenant isolation + failure behavior + docs + relevant CI.

MODE 27 — PR WORKFLOW
inspect → branch → tests → implementation → verification → docs → commit → push → PR → CI → review.
Do not merge without explicit authorization.

MODE 28 — PRIORITY
P0 repository foundation/security/tenancy/database/provider abstraction.
P1 affiliate/catalog/campaign/links/content/image/video/approval/publishing.
P2 attribution/analytics/trends/opportunity/automation.
P3 experimentation/learning/autonomous optimization.

MODE 29 — FIRST BOUNDED EXECUTION
Inspect repo/branch/open work/CI, create gap analysis, generate/update core docs, create normalized domain model and provider capability abstraction, tests first, minimal implementation, run tests/security, report status and STOP.

FINAL END-STATE
Full-stack, multi-tenant, secure, observable, policy-controlled Affiliate Content & Commerce OS.
